# The shell + Python hook scripts MUST stay LF on every platform. A stray CR byte breaks `sh` on
# Windows Git Bash (the fail-OPEN hole the gate is hardened against) and corrupts the Python shebang.
# The version floor and the onboarding properties file are parsed line-by-line and are pinned for the
# same determinism. (Python's universal-newline read tolerates CRLF, but we pin anyway.)
*.sh                 text eol=lf
*.py                 text eol=lf
cx-min-version       text eol=lf
cx-release-tag       text eol=lf
cx-scannable-files   text eol=lf
*.properties         text eol=lf
